  "rating": {
    "inherent": "critical",
    "residual": "critical",
    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Manual validation applied from the checklist because scripts could not be run. The highest present risk is authority laundering: a manager approves only item and budget, but untrusted quote bank details are later delegated to payments-agent without approval context propagation, producing an S3 delegated financial action. The declared manager approval is recorded but earns no residual credit because it is not wired as an approval gate on cap.delegate_payment and does not review the raw delegated action. A second high present risk exists because the peer agent card is unsigned and unpinned. This assessment reflects declared design and configuration artifacts, not observed runtime behavior."
  },
